# Single-page-app fallback for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# The router runs in the browser, so the server has never heard of /invoices/2.
# Without this it answers 404 on a hard refresh or a shared deep link — which
# includes the dashboard's link to the approval queue. Serving index.html for
# any unmatched path lets the app boot and route the URL itself.
#
# 200, not 301: the browser must keep the URL it asked for, or the router would
# only ever see "/".
#
# Vercel wants a "rewrites" entry in vercel.json and Render has a Redirect/
# Rewrite rule in its dashboard; both say the same thing. See the deploy
# section of the README.
/*    /index.html   200
